# Unity C# Conventions

## Patterns in this project
- `MonoBehaviour` with serialized public fields and `[Header]` groups
- Singletons: `public static X Instance { get; private set; }` set in `Awake`
- Input: New Input System — `PlayerInput` actions on Tim; `Keyboard.current` for camera keys
- Find references: `FindFirstObjectByType<T>()` (not deprecated `FindObjectOfType`)

## Do
- Match naming/style of the file you're editing
- Use `[DefaultExecutionOrder]` only when power-system ordering requires it
- Keep editor scripts in `Assets/Scripts/Editor/`
- Comment non-obvious logic (power BFS, face invalidation, camera angle mapping)

## Don't
- Revive or copy from `Assets/Legacy/*.txt`
- Rename Runode/Power types without explicit user request
- Add assembly definitions, heavy abstractions, or error handling for impossible states
- Edit `.unity`/`.prefab` YAML unless user confirms — prefer telling them Inspector wiring

## After changes
Tell user what to test in Play mode. If errors occur, ask for full Unity Console output.
